---
/**
 * The changelog (docs/decisions.md D29, D31).
 *
 * Freshness is structural, not promised: a dated list of what actually changed, written
 * by hand, with the things that are still missing named on the same page. A site that
 * quietly stops being updated is worse than one that says what it has not done yet.
 *
 * Newest first. Entries are appended, never rewritten — the same rule as the decisions log.
 */
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import ChapterFurniture from "../components/ChapterFurniture.astro";
import { SITE_HOST } from "../lib/site";

import { ENTRIES, MISSING, fmtDate as fmt } from "../lib/updates";
---

<Page
  title="Updates"
  description={`A dated changelog for ${SITE_HOST} — what changed, when, and what is still missing.`}
>
  <ChapterFurniture
    eyebrow="Updates"
    title="Updates"
    subtitle="What changed on this site, and when. Newest first."
  />

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">
        This is a changelog for the website. The printed book does not change between print
        runs — if you are holding one and a page number here does not match, that is what
        <a href="/editions">editions</a> is for.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="log">
    <h2 id="log">The log</h2>

    {
      ENTRIES.map((e) => (
        <article class="entry">
          <p class="entry__date">
            <time datetime={e.date}>{fmt(e.date)}</time>
          </p>
          <h3 class="entry__title">{e.title}</h3>
          <ul class="entry__items">
            {e.items.map((i) => (
              <li>{i}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="missing">
    <h2 id="missing">What is missing right now</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Named here rather than left for you to discover. Each one becomes a dated entry
        above when it lands.
      </p>
      <ul class="plain">{MISSING.map((m) => <li>{m}</li>)}</ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="how">
    <h2 id="how">How this page works</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Entries are written by hand and appended, never edited after the fact. If something
        on this site turns out to be wrong, the correction gets its own dated entry saying
        what was wrong — not a quiet fix.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can follow this page without giving anyone anything:{" "}
        <a href="/updates.xml">the feed is here</a>. Paste that address into any feed
        reader. There is no newsletter and there will not be one — a newsletter needs an
        email address from a thirteen-year-old, which is the one thing this site exists not
        to ask for. A feed needs no account, no address and no permission, and we have no
        way of knowing you subscribed.
      </p>
      {/* The pace note. A review asked for this and it is purely protective of the person at
          the centre of the project: a thirteen-year-old with a book out will be asked for
          more, faster, by people who mean well. Saying the pace out loud, in public, on the
          page that records every change, makes it a stated policy rather than something he
          has to defend one email at a time. */}
      <p>
        There is no schedule here. Ryan is thirteen, he is at school, and he races. Things
        get added when they are ready and not before, which sometimes means nothing changes
        for weeks. That is the pace, not a backlog — and the gap between entries is not a
        sign that something is wrong.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>

<style>
  .wrap {
    max-inline-size: 72rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: clamp(1.25rem, 5vw, 3rem);
  }

  .prose {
    max-inline-size: var(--container-measure);
  }

  .prose p + p,
  .prose ul {
    margin-block-start: 0.9em;
  }

  .lede {
    margin-block-start: 1.75rem;
    font-size: var(--text-subtitle);
    line-height: var(--text-subtitle--line-height);
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .section {
    margin-block-start: 3rem;
  }

  .section > h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    line-height: var(--text-h2--line-height);
    color: var(--text-section);
    max-inline-size: var(--container-measure);
  }

  .section > .prose {
    margin-block-start: 0.75rem;
  }

  .entry {
    max-inline-size: var(--container-measure);
    margin-block-start: 1.5rem;
    padding-block-start: 1.25rem;
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--rule-hairline);
  }

  .entry__date {
    font-size: var(--text-meta);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: var(--text-label--letter-spacing);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    /* A changelog is a column of dates; they line up. */
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums slashed-zero;
  }

  .entry__title {
    margin-block-start: 0.35rem;
    font-size: var(--text-subtitle);
    line-height: var(--text-subtitle--line-height);
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .entry__items,
  .plain {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .entry__items {
    margin-block-start: 0.75rem;
  }

  .entry__items li,
  .plain li {
    padding-block: 0.55rem;
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--rule-hairline);
  }

  a {
    text-decoration-color: currentColor;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  a:hover {
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent-spine);
  }
</style>
